The files in this folder are derived from the Chronos models by Amazon
Science (github.com/amazon-science/chronos-forecasting, Apache License 2.0,
full text in LICENSE). davesgames.io made these changes:

  chronos-bolt-tiny.fp16w.onnx
      An ONNX export of the core network of amazon/chronos-bolt-tiny
      (Hugging Face revision a0e552de83495b5c28c14c71c374f3e33280b340):
      the patch embedding, the T5 encoder and decoder, and the output
      head. The scaling, patching and unscaling are not in the graph
      (the page does them in model-io.js). Each large weight is stored as
      float16 and cast to float32 in the graph, so the file is half the
      size. The forecasts are not bit-identical to the original model.

  chronos-bolt-mini.hf.onnx, chronos-2-small.hf.onnx
      ONNX exports of the core networks of amazon/chronos-bolt-mini
      (revision 251268337516a88e253628c43e1d26ec577b376b) and
      autogluon/chronos-2-small (revision
      ddec01313e50b6bc58ebaa92ede81bc24a3d9f9a), with no weights inside.
      Each weight is an external-data reference into the unchanged
      model.safetensors of that revision, which the page fetches from
      Hugging Face at run time and checks by sha256.

The export, the parity checks and the test fixtures are in ../tools/.
